---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How We Build — The Stack Build Method | Stack10"
  description="The exact process behind every Stack Build engagement. Four phases. Senior engineers only. Security from sprint one. Production-ready AI in eight weeks."
  canonicalUrl="https://stack10.ai/how-we-build/"
>

  <!-- ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="svc-hero hero-dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-hero-inner animate-fade-up">
        <span class="section-label svc-hero-label">The Stack Build Method</span>
        <h1 class="svc-hero-title">Most AI projects stall at the architecture meeting. Ours are in production by week eight.</h1>
        <p class="svc-hero-subtitle">Speed without shortcuts. Security without afterthoughts. This is the exact process behind every Stack Build engagement — documented, repeatable, and designed around the specific points where AI projects slow down.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            Book a Discovery Call
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7"/><path d="M7 7h10v10"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/build/" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">
            See Stack Build
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── INTRO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-intro-block">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="method-intro">
        <p class="method-intro-text">Every Stack Build engagement follows the same four-phase structure. It exists because we have learned precisely where enterprise AI projects lose time — and we have engineered each of those bottlenecks out. The result is not luck. It is architecture.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── THE METHOD ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">The method</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Four phases. Every engagement.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">No exceptions. No shortcuts. This is the structural reason we ship in eight weeks when others are still in planning.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="method-phases">

        <div class="method-phase">
          <div class="method-phase-meta">
            <span class="method-phase-number">01</span>
            <div class="method-phase-label">
              <h3 class="method-phase-name">Architect First</h3>
              <span class="method-phase-weeks">Weeks 1–2</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card method-phase-card">
            <p class="method-phase-desc">Before a line of code is written, the build plan is locked. Data access is provisioned. Security architecture is defined. Story points are confirmed against technical reality — not scope assumptions. This is where most engagements are already two weeks behind us: they start building before they know what they are building.</p>
            <ul class="method-phase-list">
              <li>Production data access secured and environment provisioned</li>
              <li>Security and compliance architecture defined — data residency, access controls, audit trails</li>
              <li>Story points confirmed against actual technical constraints, not scope assumptions</li>
              <li>Integration dependencies mapped against your enterprise systems</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="method-phase">
          <div class="method-phase-meta">
            <span class="method-phase-number">02</span>
            <div class="method-phase-label">
              <h3 class="method-phase-name">Core Build</h3>
              <span class="method-phase-weeks">Weeks 3–4</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card method-phase-card">
            <p class="method-phase-desc">Working software ships at the end of week four. Not a prototype. Not a wireframe. A functioning AI system running on your actual production data, deployed in your environment. Senior engineers own every sprint. No juniors on delivery, ever.</p>
            <ul class="method-phase-list">
              <li>Working AI system built on real production data</li>
              <li>Every sprint closes with deployed, testable software — not a Jira ticket</li>
              <li>Compliance controls embedded in the data layer from day one</li>
              <li>Weekly demo to a single stakeholder — no approval chains</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="method-phase">
          <div class="method-phase-meta">
            <span class="method-phase-number">03</span>
            <div class="method-phase-label">
              <h3 class="method-phase-name">Integrate &amp; Harden</h3>
              <span class="method-phase-weeks">Weeks 5–6</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card method-phase-card">
            <p class="method-phase-desc">Enterprise integrations are complex. This phase handles them — SAP, Salesforce, Microsoft, legacy systems — while a full security review runs in parallel. Not as a final gate. In parallel. Security findings get resolved before go-live, not after.</p>
            <ul class="method-phase-list">
              <li>Enterprise integrations completed and tested under production load</li>
              <li>Full security review running concurrent with delivery — not deferred to the end</li>
              <li>Performance tested against real usage patterns</li>
              <li>Documentation written by the engineers who built it</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="method-phase">
          <div class="method-phase-meta">
            <span class="method-phase-number">04</span>
            <div class="method-phase-label">
              <h3 class="method-phase-name">Production Handover</h3>
              <span class="method-phase-weeks">Weeks 7–8</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card method-phase-card">
            <p class="method-phase-desc">The system goes live in your environment. The IP transfers. The dependency on Stack10 ends — by design. You receive the codebase, architecture docs, and runbooks to operate and extend the system internally. No retainer required. No licensing fees. No handcuff.</p>
            <ul class="method-phase-list">
              <li>System deployed to your production environment</li>
              <li>Full IP transfer — codebase, architecture documentation, runbooks</li>
              <li>Handover session with your internal team: knowledge transfer, not just file transfer</li>
              <li>Optional: Stack Build continues into ongoing Product Development</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── WHY OTHERS TAKE LONGER ────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">Structural advantage</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">It is not that other teams are slower. It is that they are structured for slowness.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Every bottleneck below is a structural property of how most AI engagements are run. The Stack Build Method was designed to remove them before a project starts.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="contrast-list">

        <div class="contrast-row">
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-problem">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">What slows others down</span>
            <p>Scope is defined after the project starts — often in week two or three, by which point assumptions are already baked into the estimate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-solution">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">Stack Build</span>
            <p>Story points are locked before day one. Every deliverable is agreed before a line of code is written. No scope surprises mid-engagement.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrast-row">
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-problem">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">What slows others down</span>
            <p>Junior engineers execute what seniors design — handoffs introduce errors, rework, and weeks of lost time at exactly the wrong moment.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-solution">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">Stack Build</span>
            <p>Senior engineers only, from architecture to deployment. The person who designs the system is the person who ships it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrast-row">
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-problem">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">What slows others down</span>
            <p>Security review is scheduled for the final sprint — findings at that stage can unravel weeks of delivered work and push go-live by months.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-solution">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">Stack Build</span>
            <p>Security architecture is defined in week one and enforced in every sprint. Phase 3 runs a full concurrent review — no late-stage surprises.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrast-row">
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-problem">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">What slows others down</span>
            <p>Multiple stakeholder approval chains add weeks to every decision — competing priorities, slow email threads, unclear sign-off authority.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-solution">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">Stack Build</span>
            <p>One stakeholder. Weekly demos. One decision point per sprint. The engagement is structured so that slowness has nowhere to hide.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrast-row">
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-problem">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">What slows others down</span>
            <p>Working code is delivered at the end — meaning real feedback arrives in week eight, when rework is most expensive and most disruptive.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="contrast-col contrast-solution">
            <span class="contrast-col-label">Stack Build</span>
            <p>Every sprint closes with deployed, testable software. Feedback arrives in week two — when it is still cheap and fast to act on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── COMPLIANCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">Built for regulated environments</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Compliance is not a checklist. It is an architectural constraint.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Enterprises operating under APRA CPS 230, AML/CTF requirements, or internal governance frameworks do not just need working code — they need code that can withstand a regulatory audit the day after it is deployed. The Stack Build Method treats compliance as a first-sprint requirement, not a post-deployment task.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="compliance-grid">

        <div class="card compliance-card">
          <div class="compliance-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M3 5v6c0 1.657 4.03 3 9 3s9-1.343 9-3V5"/><path d="M3 11v6c0 1.657 4.03 3 9 3s9-1.343 9-3v-6"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="compliance-title">Data Residency by Default</h3>
          <p class="compliance-desc">Your data stays where it is required to. Environment architecture is scoped to your regulatory constraints before a single model is trained — not negotiated with IT security in week seven.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card compliance-card">
          <div class="compliance-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/><polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="compliance-title">Audit Trails Built In</h3>
          <p class="compliance-desc">Every decision your AI system makes is logged and traceable. Designed into the data layer in Phase 1. Not added later when a compliance team raises a finding at go-live.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card compliance-card">
          <div class="compliance-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="compliance-title">Access Controls from Day One</h3>
          <p class="compliance-desc">Role-based access, authentication, and least-privilege data access are part of the architecture design — not a post-deployment hardening task added under deadline pressure.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── PROOF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-proof-callout">
        <div class="svc-proof-stat">98%</div>
        <p class="svc-proof-text">A PE-backed Australian healthcare group engaged Stack Build to ship four interconnected AI systems — an intelligence layer, a compliance agent, Xero reconciliation, and a procurement workflow. The result: <strong>98% reduction in manual compliance processing</strong> within the first quarter. All four systems are APRA-compliant and running in production today — built and handed over in under ten weeks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-dark-block">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-cta-inner">
        <h2 class="svc-cta-title">See the method applied to your problem.</h2>
        <p class="svc-cta-desc">A Discovery Call is sixty minutes. We will map your use case against the Stack Build Method and tell you exactly where your current approach is losing time — whether you engage us or not.</p>
        <div class="svc-cta-guarantees">
          <span class="svc-cta-guarantee">Fixed fee — cost agreed before work starts</span>
          <span class="svc-cta-guarantee">Senior engineers only — no juniors on delivery</span>
          <span class="svc-cta-guarantee">Full IP transfer — everything built is yours</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          Book a Discovery Call
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7"/><path d="M7 7h10v10"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── RELATED ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-related-header">
        <span class="section-label">Put the method to work</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Ready to start?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-related-cards">
        <a href="/services/build/" class="card card-clickable svc-related-card">
          <div class="svc-related-card-tag">
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Stack Build</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="svc-related-card-title">See engagement formats and pricing</h3>
          <p class="svc-related-card-desc">Senior AI engineers, story-point pricing, full IP transfer. Start with a Proof of Concept or move straight into Product Development.</p>
          <span class="svc-related-card-link">
            See Stack Build
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </a>
        <a href="/services/discover/" class="card card-clickable svc-related-card">
          <div class="svc-related-card-tag">
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Stack Discover</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="svc-related-card-title">Not sure what to build yet?</h3>
          <p class="svc-related-card-desc">Stack Discover surfaces the AI opportunities worth building before a line of code is written. Arrive at Stack Build with a validated brief, not an assumption.</p>
          <span class="svc-related-card-link">
            Learn about Stack Discover
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .svc-hero {
    background: var(--gray-1000);
    color: var(--gray-50);
    padding: var(--space-24) 0 var(--space-20);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
  }

  .svc-hero-inner {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .svc-hero-label {
    color: var(--green-400);
    border-color: oklch(0.76 0.21 150 / 0.3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5.5vw, var(--size-6xl));
    font-weight: var(--weight-800);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--gray-0);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-hero-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2vw, var(--size-xl));
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    color: var(--gray-400);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .svc-hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* ── Intro block ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .section-intro-block {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .method-intro {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .method-intro-text {
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2vw, var(--size-xl));
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Method phases ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .method-phases {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .method-phase {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .method-phase-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .method-phase-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-5xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-800);
    color: var(--primary-text);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .method-phase-label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .method-phase-name {
    font-size: var(--size-xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .method-phase-weeks {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .method-phase-card {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .method-phase-desc {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .method-phase-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .method-phase-list li {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.55;
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    position: relative;
  }

  .method-phase-list li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
  }

  /* ── Contrast list ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .contrast-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .contrast-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .contrast-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .contrast-col {
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .contrast-problem {
    background: var(--background);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .contrast-solution {
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  .contrast-col-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .contrast-problem .contrast-col-label {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .contrast-solution .contrast-col-label {
    color: var(--primary-text);
  }

  .contrast-col p {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .contrast-problem p {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .contrast-solution p {
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
  }

  /* ── Compliance cards ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .section-muted {
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  .compliance-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .compliance-card {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .compliance-icon {
    width: 2.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: var(--muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-12);
    color: var(--primary-text);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .compliance-title {
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .compliance-desc {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Social proof callout ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  .svc-proof-callout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-8);
  }

  .svc-proof-stat {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-5xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-800);
    color: var(--primary-text);
    line-height: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .svc-proof-text {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
    align-self: center;
  }

  .svc-proof-text strong {
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-weight: var(--weight-600);
  }

  /* ── CTA band ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .section-dark-block {
    background: var(--gray-950);
    color: var(--gray-50);
  }

  .svc-cta-inner {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .svc-cta-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, var(--size-4xl));
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--gray-50);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .svc-cta-desc {
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    color: var(--gray-400);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .svc-cta-guarantees {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .svc-cta-guarantee {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    color: var(--gray-300);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
